00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:06.050
Inside, the earth is rock, which is divided into the core, the mantle, and the crust.

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:11.670
Under volcanoes, forces in the earth heat the rock until it melts.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:15.490
Melted rock is called magma.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:20.450
Magma rises into chambers about a mile beneath the surface of the earth.

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:29.190
When they fill up, magma forces its way up through the volcano until the volcano explodes.

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:39.080
magma or lava pours out. It runs down the mountain, coating its slopes with new layers of rock.

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:48.130
When the eruption is over, the magma sinks back into the chambers again. In time, wind, rain,

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:53.670
and sun break down the new blanket of rock, turning it into fertile, life-giving soil.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:59.840
Trees, plants, and animals return to live there. There are 600 active volcanoes

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.150
in the world today, but only three are in Hawaii.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:06.900
